## Original Content
Voters in at least six states will soon decide ballot measures related to voter ID — the largest number of voter ID measures in a single year. The tally includes three prominent swing states.

## Summary
Voters in at least six states will decide on voter ID ballot measures this year, marking the largest number of such measures in any single year. The tally includes three prominent swing states, indicating the issue's political impact.

## Key Points
- At least six states will hold voter ID ballot measures this year.
- This is the highest number of voter ID measures in a single year historically.
- Three prominent swing states are included, affecting potential national election outcomes.


